      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Latent-space CV playground\n\nChannel-agnostic cv2 wrappers accept a LATENT directly and echo a LATENT back - every op below runs on the raw float32 latent (no uint8 quantization, no VAE round trip between steps). Coordinates and sizes count latent CELLS (pixels / 8); 'CV Array Size' reads them off any latent.\n\nTOP ROW (needs a VAE checkpoint): a photo is VAE-encoded, then rotated about its center (cv2.getRotationMatrix2D + cv2.warpAffine, dsize wired from CV Array Size) and Gaussian-blurred IN LATENT SPACE, and only then decoded - compare against the plain encode/decode round trip next to it. Rotate with warpAffine: cv2 caps rotate/transpose at 4 channels, warpAffine is channel-agnostic.\n\nBOTTOM ROWS (run without any model): an EmptyLatentImage made non-constant with CV Scalar arithmetic and a constant-9 border, then rotated and mixed back onto itself with cv2.addWeighted and blurred - all as a LATENT."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
